@startuml
title ShardingSphere-JDBC First Mode - Shared Logical DataSource

autonumber
skinparam shadowing false
hide footbox

actor "Business Service" as Service
participant "Sharding Route Context\n(optional)" as RouteContext
participant "Spring TransactionManager" as TX
participant "Business Mapper\n(MyBatis)" as MyBatis
participant "JdbcIdempotencyStorage" as IdemStorage
participant "RelationalTemplate" as RT
participant "SpringTransactionAware\nConnectionProvider" as Provider
database "ShardingSphereDataSource\n(logical DataSource)" as SS
collections "Physical Shards\norder_db_0..N / tables" as Shards

Service -> RouteContext : calculate/hold shardKey(orderId)
Service -> TX : begin transaction(ShardingSphereDataSource)
TX -> SS : get transaction-bound logical Connection

Service -> MyBatis : insert business_order(order_id, ...)
MyBatis -> SS : SQL contains shardKey/order_id
SS -> Shards : route/rewrite/execute business SQL

Service -> IdemStorage : markSuccess(idempotencyKey, shardKey)
IdemStorage -> RT : update(logical table SQL + shardKey condition)
RT -> Provider : acquire(context)
Provider -> SS : DataSourceUtils.doGetConnection(logical DataSource)
SS --> Provider : same transaction-bound logical Connection
RT -> SS : SQL contains shardKey/order_id
SS -> Shards : route/rewrite/execute idempotency SQL

alt all success
  TX -> SS : COMMIT
else any failure
  TX -> SS : ROLLBACK
end

note right of SS
ShardingSphere-JDBC is the routing/rewrite/execute engine.
Iron Relational Access treats it as a normal DataSource.
end note

note right of IdemStorage
In this mode the idempotency SQL must carry the shard key.
Otherwise ShardingSphere may not route precisely.
end note

@enduml
